WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.529
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Sunday, November eighth.

2
00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:12.309
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:13.933
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:29.690
Today: a deadly mass shooting in Krakow's main square, falling debris damaging an Aramco building in Riyadh, U.S. strikes and a disabled ship in the Iran blockade, a heavy Russian missile strike on Kyiv, and a deadly attack on a lawmaker in Guatemala.

5
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.136
We start with Poland.

6
00:00:31.136 --> 00:00:38.081
Reuters reports a gunman shooting from a car killed six people in Krakow's historic main square on Saturday afternoon.

7
00:00:38.081 --> 00:00:47.364
Authorities said seventeen people were wounded, including two police officers and the gunman, and the suspect's parents and sister were later found dead at their home.

8
00:00:47.364 --> 00:00:51.696
Authorities said the attack was likely inspired by far right ideology.

9
00:00:51.696 --> 00:01:00.535
Poland began two days of national mourning today, police have bolstered security, and police in Warsaw strengthened measures in crowded tourist areas.

10
00:01:00.535 --> 00:01:01.035
The U.K.

11
00:01:01.035 --> 00:01:05.118
Foreign Office updated its Poland travel advice following the shooting.

12
00:01:05.118 --> 00:01:07.028
Next, Saudi Arabia.

13
00:01:07.028 --> 00:01:12.835
Reuters reports an Aramco building in Riyadh was damaged by falling debris after an attempted attack, according to the ministry.

14
00:01:12.835 --> 00:01:27.849
The Institute for the Study of War says the Houthis continued to target Saudi critical infrastructure on Friday and Saturday, and that Saudi Arabia intercepted a Houthi drone and cruise missile launched toward Riyadh on Friday, November sixth.

15
00:01:27.849 --> 00:01:30.449
Turning to Iran and the Strait of Hormuz.

16
00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:44.190
The Institute for the Study of War says the United States conducted limited strikes on Iranian air defenses on Qeshm Island on Friday, November sixth, amid continued Iranian drone, missile and limpet mine attacks on commercial vessels.

17
00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:44.907
Radio Free Europe reports U.S.

18
00:01:44.907 --> 00:01:54.672
Central Command said it fired on and disabled a commercial ship whose crew ignored repeated warnings and tried to violate the naval blockade against Iran.

19
00:01:54.672 --> 00:02:00.958
Reuters also reports exclusively that the U.S. military is looking to restrict Iranian land commerce.

20
00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:02.034
In Ukraine.

21
00:02:02.034 --> 00:02:12.587
The Institute for the Study of War says Russian forces targeted Kyiv with thirty six ballistic missiles overnight Friday into Saturday as part of their campaign against energy infrastructure.

22
00:02:12.587 --> 00:02:23.590
Radio Free Europe reports Russian attacks on the power system in the Dnipropetrovsk region have left six hundred thousand people without electricity, with hospitals running on diesel generators.

23
00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:24.903
And in Guatemala.

24
00:02:24.903 --> 00:02:30.317
Reuters reports a Guatemalan lawmaker and three police officers were killed in an armed attack.

25
00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:32.517
Now a few quick notes by region.

26
00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:41.101
In the Middle East and North Africa, Reuters reports Egypt has reopened its embassy in Libya's capital, Tripoli, after a twelve year closure.

27
00:02:41.101 --> 00:02:48.770
Radio Free Europe reports Iran executed three men arrested in connection with the January anti government protests in Karaj.

28
00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:53.521
And Reuters reports heavy rain flooded tents housing displaced people in Gaza.

29
00:02:53.521 --> 00:03:04.380
In South Asia, Tribal News Network reports, citing the district police chief, that a police constable was killed by an improvised explosive device in Pakistan's Shangla district.

30
00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:14.266
And in cyber, the Italian daily La Repubblica reports the company building the Brenner Base Tunnel between Austria and Italy has confirmed it was hit by a cyberattack.

31
00:03:14.266 --> 00:03:15.708
That's today's brief.

32
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:24.025
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

33
00:03:24.025 --> 00:03:32.308
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

34
00:03:32.308 --> 00:03:34.434
This brief is digitally narrated.

35
00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:35.417
Questions?

36
00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:38.977
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

37
00:03:38.977 --> 00:03:40.972
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
